{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeGramFactorial","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeGramFactorial","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RegTraceGram","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerFactorial"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_gram_det_eq_qFactorial_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_gram_det_eq_qFactorial_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeGramFactorial.lean#L66-L79","doc":"**The substrate specialisation (sorry-free).**  For the real\nsubstrate `q > 1`, genericity is automatic, so a real algebra whose\nregular-trace Gram determinant is `c · [n]_q!` (unit `c`) is\nsemisimple.  This is the shape in which the substrate `q₀ ≈ 1.10998`\ndischarges the semisimplicity leg of the `P ≠ NP`-in-QOU counting\nargument, once the `T_w`-basis determinant is supplied. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_gram_det_eq_qFactorial_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_gram_det_eq_qFactorial_one","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeGramFactorial.lean#L54-L64","doc":"**The exact-value case `det(Gram) = [n]_q!` ⇒ semisimple\n(sorry-free).**  The unit specialises to `c = 1`: if the Gram\ndeterminant is *exactly* the quantum factorial, a Wenzl-generic `q`\nmakes `A` semisimple. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_gram_det_eq_qFactorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_gram_det_eq_qFactorial","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeGramFactorial.lean#L38-L52","doc":"**`det(Gram) = c·[n]_q!` (unit `c`) + generic ⇒ semisimple\n(sorry-free).**  The final consumable form of the Wenzl criterion.\nA `T_w`-basis Gram computation for `H_n(q)` supplies the basis `b`, a\nunit `c`, and a proof that the regular-trace Gram determinant in `b`\nequals `c · [n]_q!`; then at any Wenzl-generic `q` the algebra is\nsemisimple.  Composes `isSemisimpleRing_of_regTraceGram_det_ne_zero`\n(det ≠ 0 ⇒ semisimple) with `qFactorial_ne_zero_iff` (generic ⇒\n`[n]_q! ≠ 0`) and `mul_ne_zero`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}